3. SEMANTIC HTML AND STRUCTURE

Issue 3.1: Proper Heading Hierarchy
WCAG Criterion: 1.3.1 Info and Relationships - Level A Severity: MINOR Status: PASSES
Analysis: - All pages use proper H1 (page title) at top - H2 for major sections - H3 for subsections where applicable - No skipped heading levels detected - Blog posts properly start with H1, subdivide with H2
Example - When Groups Get Stuck post:
&lt;h1 class="title"&gt;When Groups Get Stuck on the Wrong Problem&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;!-- Content --&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;A Crowd, A Crisis, and the Wrong Problem&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;How Groups Actually Think&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;!-- Subsections within sections are also H2 --&gt;
Recommendation: MAINTAIN current practice



Issue 3.2: Form Accessibility - Missing Label Association
WCAG Criterion: 1.4.1 Use of Color - Level A Severity: MAJOR Status: FAILS
Location: /blog.qmd lines 29-39 and generated /blog.html lines 274-280
&lt;form class="email-subscription-form" action="#" method="post"&gt;
  &lt;div class="subscription-container"&gt;
    &lt;input type="email" name="email" placeholder="Enter your email address" required="" class="email-input"&gt;
    &lt;button type="submit" class="subscribe-btn"&gt;Subscribe&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;p class="subscription-note"&gt;No spam, ever. Unsubscribe at any time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/form&gt;
Problems: 1. No &lt;label&gt; element - Email input not associated with a label 2. Placeholder used as pseudo-label - Placeholder text disappears on focus 3. No aria-label as fallback - Screen readers may not announce input purpose 4. Button has no focus outline - Subscribe button has no :focus styling
Impact: - Screen reader users don’t know what the input field is for - Placeholder disappears when field is focused - Button focus indicator is missing
Recommendation:
&lt;form class="email-subscription-form" action="#" method="post"&gt;
  &lt;div class="subscription-container"&gt;
    &lt;!-- IMPROVED: Add proper label --&gt;
    &lt;label for="email-input" class="visually-hidden"&gt;Email address&lt;/label&gt;
    &lt;input type="email" 
           id="email-input"
           name="email" 
           placeholder="Enter your email address" 
           required 
           class="email-input"
           aria-describedby="email-note"&gt;
    &lt;button type="submit" class="subscribe-btn"&gt;Subscribe&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
